<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anazarbus</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Anavarza</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anazarbus was an ancient city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cilicia">Cilicia</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/turkey">Turkey</a>, near the Ceyhan river. Favoured by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>, it became the metropolis of the province of Cilicia Secunda, and in the 12th century it served as an early capital of the Rubenid Armenian lords. Its ruins, with a triumphal arch and a hilltop castle, lie beside the village of Dilekkaya.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anazarbus.jpg" alt="Anazarbus" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dosseman · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anavarza_Triumphal_arch_in_Anazarbus_2754.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
